+    <section class="slide cover active" id="slide-1" data-num="01 / 15" aria-label="Cover">
+      <div class="cover-copy"><div class="kicker">East Asian cooking field guide</div><h1>Squid,<em>ten ways.</em></h1><p>One ingredient. Ten distinct techniques across Japanese, Korean, Chinese regional and Taiwanese culinary traditions.</p></div>
+      <div class="cover-image"><img src="assets/images/01-ikayaki/generate-media-replicate_z_image_turbo-1.png" alt="Charcoal-grilled glazed whole squid on a dark plate"><div class="cover-mark">10</div></div>
+    </section>
+
+    <section class="slide overview" id="slide-2" data-num="02 / 15" aria-label="Route map">
+      <div class="overview-head"><div><div class="kicker">The route</div><h2>Ten textures</h2></div><p>Move from seconds over fierce heat to a patient braise. Each route is a distinct way to control moisture, browning and tenderness.</p></div>
+      <div class="route-list">
+        <a class="route" href="#slide-4"><span>01</span><b>Charcoal grill</b><i>Japan</i></a><a class="route" href="#slide-5"><span>02</span><b>Stuff + simmer</b><i>Hokkaido</i></a>
+        <a class="route" href="#slide-6"><span>03</span><b>Spicy stir-fry</b><i>Korea</i></a><a class="route" href="#slide-7"><span>04</span><b>Blanch + dress</b><i>Korea</i></a>
+        <a class="route" href="#slide-8"><span>05</span><b>Coat + deep-fry</b><i>Cantonese</i></a><a class="route" href="#slide-9"><span>06</span><b>Steam</b><i>Cantonese</i></a>
+        <a class="route" href="#slide-10"><span>07</span><b>Red-braise</b><i>Shanghai</i></a><a class="route" href="#slide-11"><span>08</span><b>Three-cup reduce</b><i>Taiwan</i></a>
+        <a class="route" href="#slide-12"><span>09</span><b>Dry-pot toss</b><i>Sichuan</i></a><a class="route" href="#slide-13"><span>10</span><b>Tabletop poach</b><i>Northern China</i></a>
+      </div>
+    </section>
+
+    <section class="slide principles" id="slide-3" data-num="03 / 15" aria-label="Squid fundamentals">
+      <div><div class="kicker">Before the flame</div><h2>The tender window</h2><p class="lead">Squid rewards commitment: cook it very fast, or let a moist braise carry it past toughness into tenderness.</p></div>
+      <div class="laws"><div class="law"><strong>01</strong><div><h3>Dry before heat</h3><p>Surface water steals browning. Blot well after cleaning, especially before grilling or frying.</p></div></div><div class="law"><strong>02</strong><div><h3>Score the inside</h3><p>Shallow crosshatches increase sauce contact and help flat pieces curl attractively.</p></div></div><div class="law"><strong>03</strong><div><h3>Choose a lane</h3><p>Use 45–120 seconds for high heat, or 35–60 minutes for a gentle covered simmer.</p></div></div></div>
+    </section>
+
+    <section class="slide recipe" id="slide-4" data-num="04 / 15" aria-label="Ikayaki recipe">
+      <div class="photo"><img src="assets/images/01-ikayaki/generate-media-replicate_z_image_turbo-1.png" alt="Japanese grilled squid with soy ginger glaze"><div class="tradition">Japanese festival cooking</div><div class="method-no">01</div></div>
+      <div class="recipe-copy"><div class="recipe-title"><h2>Ikayaki</h2><div class="time">Prep 15 min<br>Cook 8 min</div></div><p class="dish-note">Charcoal or a ripping-hot grill gives the soy-ginger lacquer its smoky edge.</p>
+        <div class="recipe-grid"><div><div class="label">Ingredients · serves 4</div><ul class="ingredients"><li>Whole cleaned squid <b>500 g</b></li><li>Soy sauce <b>2 tbsp</b></li><li>Mirin <b>2 tbsp</b></li><li>Grated ginger <b>2 tsp</b></li><li>Neutral oil <b>1 tsp</b></li><li>Lemon wedges <b>4</b></li></ul></div><div><div class="label">Method</div><ol class="steps"><li><b>Prepare · 10 min</b> Pat squid dry; score the mantle crosswise without cutting through.</li><li><b>Glaze · 5 min</b> Mix soy, mirin and ginger. Brush half over squid.</li><li><b>Grill · 6–8 min</b> Oil a very hot grate. Grill, turning and glazing, until opaque with charred edges.</li><li><b>Rest · 2 min</b> Slice into rings; finish with lemon.</li></ol></div></div>
+        <div class="source-links"><a href="https://asianinspirations.com.au/recipes/japanese-grilled-squid-ikayaki/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Recipe source ↗</a><a class="video" href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pT1iG4RbK34" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Watch on YouTube ▶</a></div>
+      </div>
+    </section>
+
+    <section class="slide recipe" id="slide-5" data-num="05 / 15" aria-label="Ikameshi recipe">
