+      <div class="recipe-copy"><div class="recipe-title"><h2>Ikameshi</h2><div class="time">Soak 60 min<br>Cook 45 min</div></div><p class="dish-note">Rice swells inside the mantle while squid gently tenderizes in a sweet soy broth.</p>
+        <div class="recipe-grid"><div><div class="label">Ingredients · serves 4</div><ul class="ingredients"><li>Small cleaned squid <b>4</b></li><li>Glutinous rice <b>1 cup</b></li><li>Dashi stock <b>700 ml</b></li><li>Sake <b>2 tbsp</b></li><li>Soy sauce <b>4 tbsp</b></li><li>Sugar <b>1 tbsp</b></li><li>Salt <b>¼ tsp</b></li></ul></div><div><div class="label">Method</div><ol class="steps"><li><b>Soak · 60 min</b> Rinse rice until clear; cover with water, then drain.</li><li><b>Fill · 8 min</b> Spoon rice into each squid only halfway. Close with toothpicks.</li><li><b>Simmer · 35–40 min</b> Combine dashi, sake, soy, sugar and salt. Add squid; cover and simmer gently, turning twice.</li><li><b>Set · 5 min</b> Rest in broth, remove picks and slice thickly.</li></ol></div></div>
+        <div class="source-links"><a href="https://www.maff.go.jp/e/policies/market/k_ryouri/search_menu/829/index.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">MAFF recipe ↗</a><a class="video" href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=q6OYbrRDd_M" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Watch on YouTube ▶</a></div>
+      </div>
+    </section>
